WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.860
MOBILE SUIT
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY</b>

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.030
En route to Kasarelia,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.530
Üso and the others are attacked by BESPA remnants,

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.560
and Üso learned the extent of his power in the pitched battle.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.530
Üso was forced to consider that, without V2's light wings,

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.760
a great many people would have been killed.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:48.460
Kasarelia was able to have a peaceful night.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.930
BENEATH THE ULTRA-HIGH ALTITUDE ATTACK

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.130
"Beneath the Ultra-High Altitude Attack".

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.830
What?

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.000
All that playing around is going to wake everyone up.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.130
Üso?

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.960
Do you hear it?

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.400
You hear it, too?

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.130
Yeah, for a while, now.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.860
I wonder if someone's up in the sky.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.530
What the hell? Quiet down.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.460
Is it BESPA?!

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.500
Where?! Where?!

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.460
Don't you hear that bell?

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.030
Bell?

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.700
Karl seems to like it.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:12.300
Üso, we're heading for Largaine base.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.260
See you later!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:33.860
There, see? The air in the forest is slightly different, right?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.760
Yeah, I'm sort of used to it now.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.930
Your dad and the others headed over to the lake?

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.230
They said they found a cabin we could use.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.360
Üso went to Largaine?

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:48.100
They're getting a booster they found to launch the White Ark back into space.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.430
Why? He should've stayed with us.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.330
Yeah!

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.860
It's better for him if he's working.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.030
It keeps him from thinking about other stuff.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.900
All right! All right!

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.860
A little slower! You're going too fast.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.860
Mr. Otis, Miss Juca, can you run the checks, please?

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.530
Mr. Romero, are we really going back into space?

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:21.200
BESPA's using this ceasefire to buy time,

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:24.530
and the Federation's using it as an excuse to do nothing.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.630
I hope this wasn't that guy's decision.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.660
While we can't be frank about how we really feel,

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.060
in this case, his opinion is the correct one.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.300
Are those connections ready?

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:35.960
Yup.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:36.630
Okay!

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.600
Hey, that's dangerous!

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.300
He saw us!

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:44.230
Run!

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:45.930
Those girls!

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.360
Go away! Leave!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.600
Stop that!

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.860
Those men said they're the people who killed dad!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.330
They said that! They said that!

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.800
Otis, hurry it up over here, too!

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.760
Your father was a soldier.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.560
It's shameful to throw stones at people!

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.300
You'll ruin your father's name!

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.030
Pardon me, but... I'm sorry.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.560
I fought and... I'm sorry!

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.560
You're a guerrilla?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.960
Children shouldn't be participating in a war.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:25.330
So I've been told.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.360
But I don't want your sympathy.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.230
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.030
And stop helping these guerrillas. Farm the land, instead.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.530
And you shouldn't stay at this base, either.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.530
Sis just...

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.230
I'd like to leave, but...

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:40.830
Stop that!

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.400
We'll decide what we'll do.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.430
Let's go.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:50.300
Um, I... I...

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:53.200
Üso, what's up? Give us a hand.

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:53.860
Right.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.430
Miss Martina and the others are already asleep.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.960
Karl's still up.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.030
Still, sneaking into the girls' room...

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.900
Oh! What's up?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.400
Um, the toilet! Where's the toilet?

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.930
I told you, the toilet's that way!

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:16.860
For crying out loud!

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.500
I thought I was gonna have a heart attack!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.360
No kidding!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.800
Shahkti?

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.260
What are you doing with the computer bank?

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.160
There's something I want to look up.

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.600
She's studying at this hour?

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:38.230
You're looking up bells in the encyclopedia?

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:38.930
Yeah.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.660
What's up? You heard a noise like that?

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:42.600
Yeah.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.830
Huh? People condemned to the guillotine...

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.700
...had to walk through town with a bell tied to their waist?

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.130
It was a practice in olden times.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.330
Nasty.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.300
Okay!

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:01.760
Go ahead, Miss Marbet.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:05.730
Roger. We'll fly to Kasarelia for the booster test.

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:09.800
What was that?!

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.130
It came from the base's residential zone!

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.760
It looks like a beam was fired from straight above us!

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.560
Air raid!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.630
Was it the League Militaire?!

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:23.900
No!

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.430
I don't believe this!

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.930
Even though some of BESPA's people are still here!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.630
Get the Reineforce moving!

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.130
The engines are ignited!

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:34.930
Kid, where are you going?!

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.330
Come back! They'll attack again!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.800
They say the Reineforce can evacuate!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.660
No response from Üso! Where'd he go?!

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.930
Where are you?! Where are you?!

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.100
The power of that beam...!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.760
Someone's firing from a really high altitude!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:10.600
There they are!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.400
Keep your heads down!

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.500
We don't know what might come flying!

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.000
You aren't hurt! Are you okay?

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.200
You! But, why?

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.530
Don't cry. I'm going to take you someplace safe.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:24.560
I'll lead. Come on.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.160
Prepare to launch!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.130
Get us out of here before we're picked off!

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:35.000
Don't ask me for every little thing! Just launch, already!

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:48.960
Looks like they got the weapons depot.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:51.130
Let's escape on this ship.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:52.600
On this ship?

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.230
Miss Marbet, it's Üso.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.360
I'm boarding the White Ark now.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.200
I'm fleeing the base aboard a guerrilla ship?

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.700
Hurry up!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.200
Üso's back. Take off!

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.030
Roger!

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.060
The Reineforce's booster has already been tested.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.600
Time for us to test ours!

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:22.800
Are the bells getting worse?

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.160
What's wrong?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:29.100
It looks like there's been an air raid on Largaine, but I'm not sure.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.600
Üso's radio is so old!

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:48.100
You’re saying the League Militaire doesn’t have any weapons...

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:50.260
...to attack Largaine from high altitude?

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:52.200
Neither do the Federation Forces.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.660
You mean BESPA is breaking the ceasefire?!

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.700
I don't know if it's BESPA or...

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.260
Üso, we're in Kasarelia.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:00.600
Understood.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:02.060
We're landing.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:07.400
They flew here with the booster attached?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.030
What could have happened?

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:17.800
Tomáš, Odelo, can you come aboard?

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.500
Are you alone, Miss Marbet?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.530
Juca came with me. Prep your mobile suits for launch.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.300
Roger!

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:24.700
Üso, get V2 ready, as well.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.500
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.930
Before I sortie, there's someplace I want to bring you.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.300
Please, wait here!

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.830
Haro's already aboard!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:38.800
Thanks!

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.830
That white mobile suit is...

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.930
They have children piloting them?!

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.760
V1 is moving out, too!

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.930
If that child is the pilot,

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.930
then that explains everything he's been saying.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:03.730
Mama!

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:05.800
What?!

00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:10.730
Please, get in the hand. I'll take you.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.460
W-Where to?

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.930
To... To your husband's...

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.660
...grave, Ma'am.

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.700
I'll rendezvous once I take Mrs. Lena.

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:40.430
Roger.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:50.760
Wow!

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:52.560
It's so dark below us!

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:07.030
Graves...

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.430
It's the ninth one from you.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:47.830
That nice boy told us where your father's grave is.

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.500
Papa's?!

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:52.000
He killed him, didn't he?!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.060
Whoever killed your papa...

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.700
...wouldn't tell us where his grave is, right?

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:02.330
You mustn't accuse people of bad things so easily.

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.530
Y-Yes.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:04.630
Mama?

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.530
From now on, your papa will be in the sky,

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:09.900
always watching over you two.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:13.600
And he wouldn't like you being a bad girl, like you just were.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:25.430
It's a photo of all of us.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.860
Oh, Darling... Why?!

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:56.800
Mama!

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:57.930
Mama!

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.630
Üso? You're in there, aren't you, Üso?

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.200
Yeah.

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.660
I know how hard this is now, but be careful.

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:34.330
I will. I always am.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:35.500
That's not what I mean.

00:14:35.530 --> 00:14:38.430
I know the bell sound is something bad, now.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:40.130
What do you mean?

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.400
People who were condemned to die...

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:46.260
...were once made to walk through town with bells tied to their waist.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:47.760
I know that.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.430
While I was at Zanscare, I heard about Fuala Griffon.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:56.330
The former commander of Largaine.

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:57.800
The one who used the guillotine.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:02.600
I know. Shahkti, look after those people, please.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:04.600
Sure. Okay.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.100
Hasn't the Shrike Team caught up with us, yet?

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.430
They're targeting our ship, aren't they?

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:40.230
Which is why we're running around!

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:43.730
Captain, tip the Reineforce up! Point the shield up!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.400
The power balance is too difficult to pull that off!

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.730
We're being shot at from above!

00:15:48.760 --> 00:15:50.600
The White Ark is climbing!

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.000
Thank goodness!

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:02.700
Only one flying object detected in the stratosphere!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:03.560
Location?

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.560
Directly overhead. It isn't a ship or a mobile suit.

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:07.800
Put it onscreen.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.600
Right.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:09.860
A flying saucer?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.300
The bell sounds are getting closer.

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:14.630
I'm taking command today. All right with you?

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.200
Of course, Miss Juca.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:19.100
We'll have Marbet use the White Ark's cannon.

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:20.730
All units, prepare to launch.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.860
The enemy's concentrating on the Reineforce right now.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.000
We're going to buy them time to escape.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.800
Shouldn't we take the initiative?

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.700
Figuring out what we're dealing with comes first!

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.230
Entering firing range.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.060
Prepare to fire the mega particle cannon!

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:34.930
Roger!

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:42.200
Gun Blasters, move out!

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:43.730
This headache...

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.000
Go!

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.700
It's so fast!

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.000
The bells are ringing...

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.230
But...!

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.430
Target the ring from below!

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.460
A barrier, beneath it, too?!

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.700
Tomáš!

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:15.300
The head's just for looks, anyway!

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:20.660
Are those crescents on the shoulders just for show?

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:27.230
It has beams there, too?!

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.830
We're still being targeted!

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:47.960
Can't Marbet and the others give us some cover?!

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:51.900
Odelo, let's help Marbet use the cannon!

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:52.930
Roger!

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:56.000
Right! If you can just distract it!

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:03.000
Can this thing just climb anywhere?!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.400
Miss Juca, you're climbing too high!

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:10.000
With flight ability like that, it must have come from space!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.930
It's no ordinary mobile suit!

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.630
You're not getting away.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.730
Now fall!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.430
Elisha!

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:28.830
What a beam cannon!

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:29.760
Sis!

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:31.360
My head's aching!

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:32.760
We're descending!

00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:37.500
Marbet! What's wrong?!

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:44.900
I'm in!

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.100
I'm not done yet!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:55.900
It'll take more than that!

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:03.830
It's glowing!

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.630
Huh? It's retreating?

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:06.430
What?!

00:19:06.460 --> 00:19:07.330
Really?

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:19.760
How's it look, Odelo?

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.500
The control lines weren't destroyed,

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.530
so we just swap on a head and we're done.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.960
We're to fly into space immediately?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.500
BESPA is on the move in full!

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.230
One of us is injured!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:35.260
And the Gun Blaster's head needs to be replaced!

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.500
If BESPA did this during their ceasefire, then...

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.960
I understand that!

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:43.860
We've faced enemies like that, so we'll go to space.

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:46.330
But some of us are still in Kasarelia!

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:49.330
Just give us a little time!

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:51.600
There's a ton of things I'd like to do, but...

00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:53.060
Please, Captain!

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.830
Since they're fighting for the home that they love,

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.260
they need some time to say goodbye to it!

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.230
This is no time for sentimental talk!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.760
Zanscare's BESPA is...

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.800
Fine!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:07.730
We need to resupply, as well. One day's leave!

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.260
Thank you, sir!

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:16.700
You better come back!

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:19.460
We'll clean the house up for you! Good luck!

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:23.560
Take care!

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.530
We'll come back! We promise!

00:20:25.560 --> 00:20:28.530
Take care! Don't do anything stupid!

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:33.160
I didn't see Miss Elisha. Does she still not feel well?

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:35.130
She probably shouldn't exert herself.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:40.530
You idiots! You don't need to do this!

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:43.600
Everyone, get that house fixed up for us!

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.300
My room, too!

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:49.060
Weren't we going to meet again in Kasarelia?

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:52.660
This is nothing compared to the battles we've seen already!

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:53.700
Exactly.

00:20:55.030 --> 00:20:56.900
Mom, I'm off.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:58.500
Next time...

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.560
They told me you lost your mother.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:05.800
Y-Yes.

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:18.830
You've led me to a nice place.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:22.200
There's a nice cabin toward the lake.

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.400
Your husband...

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:25.230
Hm?

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.400
Well, if you'll excuse me.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:34.800
May you have good fortune in battle.

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:36.900
Yes, ma'am. Thank you very much.

00:21:45.330 --> 00:21:47.630
Üso's aboard, Captain Marbet.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:50.400
Roger! Say farewell to Kasarelia!

00:23:30.530 --> 00:23:33.460
Awaiting us as we launch back into space...

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:36.260
...is the mobile suit with its terrible beam...

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:38.330
...and the sound of bells.

00:23:38.660 --> 00:23:44.200
Üso spreads V2's wings and leads us,

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:47.230
but there's an unexpected reunion...

00:23:47.430 --> 00:23:50.200
...at Hiland where the fleet is gathering.

00:23:50.300 --> 00:23:53.500
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:56.630
Next Episode THE BATTLEFIELD THAT FATHER MADE
"The Battlefield That Father Made".

00:23:56.630 --> 00:23:58.160
Please watch it!

00:23:58.160 --> 00:23:59.760
Next Episode THE BATTLEFIELD THAT FATHER MADE
